parameters.text:
=Meeting title: {{ $json.data.transcript.title }}
Meeting date: {{ $json.data.transcript.date }}
Meeting summary and action items: {{ $json.data.transcript.summary.action_items }}
Meeting overview: {{ $json.data.transcript.summary.overview }}

Extract all action items from this meeting. Return ONLY a raw JSON array — no markdown, no explanation, no code fences. Each object must have exactly these keys:
- task_title: actionable task starting with a verb (e.g. "Send revised proposal to client")
- assignee: person name extracted from context, or "Unassigned"
- deadline: ISO date YYYY-MM-DD, infer from urgency language, default to 7 days from today if unclear
- priority: "High", "Medium", or "Low" based on urgency language
- notes: one sentence of context explaining why this task matters

Today is {{ $now.toFormat('yyyy-MM-dd') }}.

parameters.jsCode:
const agentOutput = $input.first().json.output || '';
const transcript = $('Fetch Transcript from Fireflies').first().json.data.transcript;
const meetingTitle = transcript.title || 'Unknown Meeting';
const meetingDate = transcript.date || '';

let items = [];
const cleaned = agentOutput
  .replace(/```json\n?/g, '')
  .replace(/```\n?/g, '')
  .trim();
const startIdx = cleaned.indexOf('[');
const endIdx = cleaned.lastIndexOf(']');
if (startIdx !== -1 && endIdx !== -1) {
  items = JSON.parse(cleaned.substring(startIdx, endIdx + 1));
}

return items.map(function(item) {
  return {
    json: {
      task_title: item.task_title || 'Untitled Task',
      assignee: item.assignee || 'Unassigned',
      deadline: item.deadline || '',
      priority: item.priority || 'Medium',
      notes: item.notes || '',
      meeting_title: meetingTitle,
      meeting_date: meetingDate
    }
  };
});

